The boot loader was installed successfully. systemd-boot will automatically
generate entries for Windows, macOS and all .efi files in /boot/EFI/Linux. You
can customize the boot loader config further, if you would like. Here is an
overview of the settings we added to boot loader config and their current value:
    - default: the default entry (supporting wild cards) that will be booted if
        there is no user input at boot; set to a value determined by the script
        or to nothing if it was unsuccessful in finding a UKI to be booted
    - timeout: how long the boot menu will be shown; set to menu-hidden, which
        will not display the menu unless the space bar is held down at boot
    - editor: whether or not to allow editing the kernel command line from the
        boot menu; disabled for security
    - console-mode: resolution of the boot menu; set to max, the highest
        possible resolution

If you put UKIs in a folder other than /boot/EFI/Linux, or have other EFI
applications you would like to include in the boot menu, remember to create
entries for them manually.
